From 33359a9258bfbc57c85f8f7800069e814c4e9a4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huy3ko <hugundlach@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:27:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(belief): propagated evidence keeps one voice across
 several paths
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the observation identity. A propagated contribution belongs to
ONE originating observation, but the same observation can reach a belief over
several graph paths — and until now the entry was keyed by origin only, so the
path structure was lost:

* per-path state: each path keeps its own weight; the entry's weight is the
  strongest live path. Withdrawing the strongest path promotes the next one
  instead of erasing the whole effect.
* a re-assessed origin lowers the contribution (the path is updated) instead
  of being ignored as "weaker than what is there".
* the minimum-propagation-weight guard now only gates NEW propagation, never
  the correction or withdrawal of a path already recorded.
* a direct assertion of the same observation already speaks for the belief;
  its own propagation adds nothing, so one observation is one voice.
* ties between paths of equal magnitude are broken by source id, so neither
  the traversal order nor the polarity ordering changes the result.

Wired the origin into the engine path (`assert_belief_evidence` used the
origin-less variant, so the runtime did not deduplicate at all).

Tests: four new semantics in engine/tests/belief_propagation_identity.rs
(strongest path withdrawn, origin weakened, direct + propagated, opposite
polarity); the four existing ones stay green. All 97 belief tests pass, the
two known-decay tests remain ignored (separate patch).
